@startuml
' claim: a pin's tier comes from the pinned deb's own declaration; the fixed map only cross-checks, and never lists a product
left to right direction
rectangle "repository R\ndeps.txt: # tier: <n> <kind>" as R
rectangle "lib/deb.sh\n(build_deb.sh of the pinned repository)" as DEB
rectangle "pinned deb\nX-Kyr-Tier: <m> <kind>" as PIN
rectangle "tiers.txt\nfixed platform repositories" as MAP
rectangle "deps.sh check --tiers" as CHECK
DEB --> PIN : copies its repository's declaration
R --> CHECK : declared n
PIN --> CHECK : m, from the cached deb (sha256-verified)
MAP ..> CHECK : cross-check; stands in for a deb without the field
CHECK --> R : every pin m < n, else VIOLATION
note bottom of MAP
  unlisted repository => may only declare "5 product";
  a new product needs no line here
end note
@enduml
